      Alternative: two devices? No — slot is per device. Two install tasks for same device on different releases where both tasks are PENDING simultaneously: v1 active, t1 PENDING (not started). To have t2 on another release, v1 must be cancelled, which cancels t1 (PENDING → CANCELLED). Hmm! So how can two startable tasks for the same device coexist?

      Scenario: v1, t1 PENDING → start → INSTALLING. cancel v1 → t1 CANCEL_REQUESTED (holds slot). v2, t2 PENDING. Now concurrent: stopConfirm(t1) and start(t2) — race: if stopConfirm commits first, start succeeds; if start checks slot first → 422. That's a legit concurrency test: outcome either 422 or INSTALLING, and final slot count ≤ 1, and if start succeeded then t1 CANCELLED.

      Or: synthetic two concurrent starts for same device on different releases requires two PENDING install tasks on different releases — impossible since cancelling v1 cancels PENDING t1. Unless... createInstallTask for v1 t1 PENDING; don't cancel; can't create v2 (active_model unique). So two concurrent starts same device can't happen via different releases. Same release same device → one task only. So concurrent start race on the same slot: only via stopConfirm+start interleaving, or via two tasks... hmm, actually can two PENDING install tasks for the same device exist? Same release: unique (release,device) — no. Different releases: requires v1 cancelled → its PENDING tasks cancelled. So no. 

      But the unique index race can still occur: start(t2) checks slot free while stopConfirm(t1) in-flight... both fine. What about start(t2) concurrent with start(t2')? Same task — idempotent different requestIds: both start same task t2 concurrently → both INSTALLING (second is no-op return). Fine.

      So concurrency test: 并发停止确认与开始_槽不重叠: loop rounds: setup t1 INSTALLING (v1), cancel v1 (t1 CANCEL_REQUESTED gen1), v2, t2 PENDING. Concurrent { stopConfirm(t1, gen1), start(t2) }. Outcomes: either start 422 (slot still held at check) then... hmm if start 422, slot later released by stopConfirm; t2 remains PENDING. Or start succeeds after stopConfirm → t2 INSTALLING. Both valid; assert: final slot holders ≤ 1; if start succeeded → t1 CANCELLED and t2 INSTALLING and slot = d1 held by t2; if 422 → t2 PENDING, slot null after stopConfirm. Assert no exception other than ApiException 422. And DB unique index never violated (implicitly).

      Also direct unique-index race: hard to construct given above constraints. Skip; the 422 path is tested.

    @Test 并发回执与取消请求_唯一结局
      loop 10: v = release, t install task, start → INSTALLING
      concurrent { receipt SUCCESS, cancelRequest }
      outcome A: receipt wins → task SUCCESS, device 2.0.0, slot null, round_success 1; cancelRequest → 409 TASK_NOT_CANCELLABLE
      outcome B: cancelRequest wins → task CANCEL_REQUESTED gen 1, slot held, device 1.0.0, stats 0; receipt → 409 TASK_CANCEL_REQUESTED
      assert exactly one of the two "failed" with 409; final state consistent.

    @Test 并发停止确认_同代次只成功一次
